WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:02.386
- Oh my gosh, it's an
honor to have you here.

00:00:02.386 --> 00:00:03.219
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:03.219 --> 00:00:04.090
Thank you for coming

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:05.110
- Pleasure to having me.

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:05.943
(Yuh-jung laughs softly)

00:00:05.943 --> 00:00:08.060
- Those lines could be used many times

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:09.930
and I will be stealing them.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:12.391
Is it true that you
started acting by accident?

00:00:12.391 --> 00:00:13.390
(Yuh-jung laughs softly)

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:14.280
- It is true.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.730
- So, how does that happen?

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:17.210
- Well, it's a long story,

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.203
I will try to make it short.

00:00:19.203 --> 00:00:21.370
Please understand my language.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.639
I do have a lack of English.

00:00:23.639 --> 00:00:25.540
- I'm understanding you perfectly.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.450
- If you ask me a simple question,

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.308
I will answer it simply.

00:00:29.308 --> 00:00:33.420
In Korea, if you graded
certain high school,

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.303
you got to go a certain level of college,

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.580
Ivy League college or something,

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.472
but I didn't get in.

00:00:42.472 --> 00:00:43.305
(Yuh-jung laughs softly)

00:00:43.305 --> 00:00:45.200
So, that's very disappointing

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.400
for my family and for my mother.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.233
- Oh.

00:00:48.233 --> 00:00:51.030
- So, I felt so sorry for my mother,

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.504
I tried to look for the part-time job,

00:00:53.504 --> 00:00:57.090
but at that time back in 1960s,

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.994
my age is very old,

00:00:59.994 --> 00:01:00.827
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:03.026
it was new, television was to Korea.

00:01:03.026 --> 00:01:03.859
- Yeah.

00:01:03.859 --> 00:01:07.210
I went to kind of tour
for the television station

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.243
and one guy,

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:10.870
I met him in hallway

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.310
and then, "Would you
like to have an audition?

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:15.360
Would you like to help us doing some kind

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.880
of presenting some gift for the audience?"

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:20.600
So I said, "Okay, I'll do it.",

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:23.070
and then I was freshman year

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:26.030
and they gave me the big check,

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:27.545
so, that was very tempting.

00:01:27.545 --> 00:01:28.753
(Yuh-jung, Kelly and
audience all laughing)

00:01:28.753 --> 00:01:29.586
- Yeah,

00:01:29.586 --> 00:01:30.419
you were like, Wait,

00:01:30.419 --> 00:01:33.290
so how many more times can I
present something to someone?

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:34.410
- Yeah, exactly.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.300
- That's amazing that
that's how this all started.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.699
And you are so gifted.

00:01:37.699 --> 00:01:39.443
You are so talented.

00:01:39.443 --> 00:01:40.631
That's amazing.

00:01:40.631 --> 00:01:42.730
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:44.230
I just think it's amazing that

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:47.140
that wasn't your vocation
you were going for

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.230
and you just landed there.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.670
So, is it true...

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:51.650
I found this out that a psychic told you

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:54.665
that you would find your
soulmate at 96-years-old.

00:01:54.665 --> 00:01:55.660
(Yuh-jung laughs)

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:56.982
I have two things.

00:01:56.982 --> 00:02:01.627
One, you gotta wait till
you're 96 to find this person?

00:02:01.627 --> 00:02:04.436
And then two, congratulations.

00:02:04.436 --> 00:02:05.269
(Yuh-jung laughs)

00:02:05.269 --> 00:02:07.260
You're gonna make it to at least 96.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.317
That's amazing.

00:02:08.317 --> 00:02:09.760
(audience applauding)

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:10.967
- Actually. I asked him,

00:02:10.967 --> 00:02:15.967
do you think I can recognize
he's real soul mate at age 96?

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.022
Maybe at age 96, maybe I
get Alzheimer or senile.

00:02:22.022 --> 00:02:22.856
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:22.856 --> 00:02:23.689
- Oh my God.

00:02:23.689 --> 00:02:25.463
- How can I recognize he's soul mate?

00:02:25.463 --> 00:02:28.260
That was my question.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.093
- That's amazing.

00:02:29.093 --> 00:02:30.928
I just love that psychic.

00:02:30.928 --> 00:02:32.280
Who tells someone that?

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.420
That's amazing.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.290
So, wait, will you tell
us about your new show?

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:36.940
It seems so intense.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:37.864
What is the new show about?

00:02:37.864 --> 00:02:40.910
- Did you ever heard of Pachinko?

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:44.560
Wrote by a Korean-American also?

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:46.867
And it was, I think one time,

00:02:46.867 --> 00:02:50.000
bestseller in New York times
or something like that.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:50.833
- Yeah.

00:02:50.833 --> 00:02:51.666
- It had a good review.

00:02:51.666 --> 00:02:53.190
- I think all good shows were books, yeah.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:58.860
- Apple bought this story
back in 1909 until 1989.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.622
It's a four generation story,

00:03:04.622 --> 00:03:07.330
of course I'm playing a grandma role,

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:08.662
so, it's no problem,

00:03:08.662 --> 00:03:11.500
when I was young, the other actor,

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.753
a young actress plays my role.

00:03:16.842 --> 00:03:20.223
In that time we were occupied by Japan,

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:25.550
so during that time they
happen to went to Japan

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:30.550
and they're struggling, suffering
in that foreign country.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:35.940
That role was very...
Somehow I read the script

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:38.683
and it, really, immediate
connection with her.

00:03:38.683 --> 00:03:39.516
- It spoke to you.

00:03:39.516 --> 00:03:40.370
- Yes, yes.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:44.080
Her strength and then her determination

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.950
to survive from foreign country,

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.580
for her it's a foreign country,

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.580
she was in Korea.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:51.413
- Yeah.

00:03:51.413 --> 00:03:52.246
- Born in Korea,

00:03:52.246 --> 00:03:55.210
and then she happened to went to Japan.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:04:00.210
So, I relate to her and that's
why I wanted to do this role.

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:03.279
So I just... I thought...

00:04:03.279 --> 00:04:05.990
I'm not sure I did it okay but we'll see.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:07.010
- You did awesome,

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:08.980
and I love the fact that you brought up,

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:10.410
we wouldn't be where we are,

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:12.580
we're so lucky from our ancestors

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:13.413
that paved the way

00:04:13.413 --> 00:04:14.654
for us to have the life that we have.

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:15.487
(audience applauding)

00:04:15.487 --> 00:04:17.080
- Indeed, indeed, indeed, yes.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:17.913
- It's so important.

00:04:17.913 --> 00:04:18.746
I think we forget,

00:04:18.746 --> 00:04:20.440
a lot of us don't grow up with

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.210
that kind of family
around us, so we forget,

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:23.410
but God, how blessed we are

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:24.783
to have those people before us,

00:04:24.783 --> 00:04:26.248
so that I could be here now.

00:04:26.248 --> 00:04:27.081
- Yes, that's right.

00:04:27.081 --> 00:04:27.914
That's right, yes.

00:04:27.914 --> 00:04:28.747
(audience applauding)

00:04:28.747 --> 00:04:31.448
- Well, Pachinko is
also a game at casinos,

00:04:31.448 --> 00:04:33.120
I don't know if you gamble,

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.400
but have you ever been to Las Vegas?

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:36.233
Have you ever gambled?

00:04:36.233 --> 00:04:37.530
- Yes, I've been there

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:40.060
because my dear friend is living there,

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:42.115
so, actually she took me to that.

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:45.590
Every place just has a machine.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:46.550
- Slot machines.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:47.660
- Yes, slot machines.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:49.840
And then she said... She gave me $20

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:53.170
and then she asked me
to just push the button

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:55.300
or just pull it like this,

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:58.710
so I said to her, "It's not hygienic.",

00:04:58.710 --> 00:04:59.833
because millions of
people have touched it.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:03.095
- You're my sister,

00:05:03.095 --> 00:05:05.230
my sister, I kid you not,

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:07.389
comes in with Lysol,

00:05:07.389 --> 00:05:09.870
she wipes it down,

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.601
she's afraid of that too.

00:05:11.601 --> 00:05:13.267
- Me too, no, I don't wanna do that.

00:05:13.267 --> 00:05:14.100
(everyone laughs)

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.680
- Okay, so, thank you so much, Yuh-jung.

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:20.353
You can see Pachinko on Apple
TV plus starting tomorrow.

